{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DYNZvRcwh92JrzfYVjieWq","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Mistral API DELETE /v1/models/{model_id} model_id parameter reference\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"MistralClient.API.Models — mistralex_ai v0.1.0\",\"url\":\"https://hexdocs.pm/mistralex_ai/MistralClient.API.Models.html\"},{\"title\":\"Delete Model - Mistral AI\",\"url\":\"https://bsq57ahho8.apidog.io/api-8963131\"},{\"title\":\"Mistral AI API | Mistral AI\",\"url\":\"https://platform-docs-public.pages.dev/api/\"},{\"title\":\"openapi: 3.1.0 info: title: Mistral AI API description: >-\",\"url\":\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/wso2/apk/refs/heads/main/samples/llm-providers-oas-definitions/mistral/mistral_api.yaml\"},{\"title\":\"Model Management | mistralai/client-python | DeepWiki\",\"url\":\"https://deepwiki.com/mistralai/client-python/3.4-structured-output\"},{\"title\":\"docs.mistral.ai\",\"url\":\"https://docs.mistral.ai/api/endpoint/models\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about the Mistral API DELETE /v1/models/{model_id} endpoint and its model_id parameter:\n\n## DELETE /v1/models/{model_id} Reference\n\n**Endpoint:** DELETE /v1/models/{model_id}\n\n**Purpose:** Delete a fine-tuned model\n\n**model_id Parameter:**\n\nThe model_id is a required path parameter of type string. The example value is \"ft:open-mistral-7b:587a6b29:20240514:7e773925\" and the description is \"The ID of the model to delete.\"\n\n**Important Restrictions:**\n\n- You can only delete fine-tuned models that you own\n- Base models cannot be deleted\n\n**Response:**\n\nThe successful response (200) is in JSON format with fields for \"id\", \"object\", and \"deleted\" status\n\nThe parameter expects the model ID in the format of fine-tuned models (typically starting with \"ft:\"), not base model identifiers.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8ee12b9b-fa5c-4484-8000-10350002b058","uuid":"031dbe9f-a673-4291-94ab-3b59775efaac","timestamp":"2026-09-09T22:32:56.267Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Mistral API DELETE /v1/models/{model_id} model_id parameter reference","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01R4LKWj4Sq3bCuuwA2U1gvq","content":[{"title":"MistralClient.API.Models — mistralex_ai v0.1.0","url":"https://hexdocs.pm/mistralex_ai/MistralClient.API.Models.html"},{"title":"Delete Model - Mistral AI","url":"https://bsq57ahho8.apidog.io/api-8963131"},{"title":"Mistral AI API | Mistral AI","url":"https://platform-docs-public.pages.dev/api/"},{"title":"openapi: 3.1.0 info: title: Mistral AI API description: >-","url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/wso2/apk/refs/heads/main/samples/llm-providers-oas-definitions/mistral/mistral_api.yaml"},{"title":"Model Management | mistralai/client-python | DeepWiki","url":"https://deepwiki.com/mistralai/client-python/3.4-structured-output"},{"title":"docs.mistral.ai","url":"https://docs.mistral.ai/api/endpoint/models"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information about the Mistral API DELETE /v1/models/{model_id} endpoint and its model_id parameter:\n\n## DELETE /v1/models/{model_id} Reference\n\n**Endpoint:** DELETE /v1/models/{model_id}\n\n**Purpose:** Delete a fine-tuned model\n\n**model_id Parameter:**\n\nThe model_id is a required path parameter of type string. The example value is \"ft:open-mistral-7b:587a6b29:20240514:7e773925\" and the description is \"The ID of the model to delete.\"\n\n**Important Restrictions:**\n\n- You can only delete fine-tuned models that you own\n- Base models cannot be deleted\n\n**Response:**\n\nThe successful response (200) is in JSON format with fields for \"id\", \"object\", and \"deleted\" status\n\nThe parameter expects the model ID in the format of fine-tuned models (typically starting with \"ft:\"), not base model identifiers."],"durationSeconds":5.390146537999999,"searchCount":1}